# Tabletop UI

Tabletop is the **default** production skin. Classic is rollback-only.

Full visual authority order and anatomy details: `docs/DESIGN_AUTHORITY.md`.

## Isolation

- Import only `./tabletop.css` from the Tabletop skin entry
- Never import Classic components, helpers, or Classic stylesheets into the active Tabletop graph
- Registry may register Classic via `./classic/skin` (components only); Classic CSS lives under `./classic/styles` and must not load while `ACTIVE_SKIN_ID` is `tabletop`
- Every rule scoped under `.tabletop-skin` / `[data-skin="tabletop"]`
- No global generic selectors (`.box`, `.table`, `.dealer`, `.felt` without skin scope)
- No `!important` cascade fixes for architectural conflicts
- Remove obsolete selectors instead of layering overrides

## Visual authority

1. Original approved PNGs under `design/reference/classic/approved/`
2. Product phase/control/role contracts
3. Tabletop implementation
4. HTML prototype as secondary token colour reference only
5. Historical/implementation screenshots are never design authority

## Composition contract

- Phone composition: `100dvh`, max width ~480px, **no document scroll**
- Minimum interactive target 44×44px
- `BlackjackTableSurface` owns Blackjack table geometry: emerald felt base, curved gold rail (Shell `TableRail`), embroidered table name on the cloth (`data-felt-name` / `data-table-name`), Dealer position overlay, Player overlay layer
- Felt/table is the permanent base; Dealer and Players overlay it — never a panel containing the table, never a separate bottom table-name plaque, never a giant bordered ledger container
- Table Setup Player rows use AVAILABLE/READY — never MAIN BET / Waiting for a joined Player
- Dealer and Player devices are two viewpoints onto the same physical table (same rail, felt, name, Dealer position, vertical proportions)
- No title-card name, no duplicated name, no giant empty bordered rectangle, no yellow centre divider
- Stable anatomy across phase transitions: same felt/rail/header/dock allocation; phases change labels, values, and legal controls — never replace the table furniture
- `prefers-reduced-motion` must not rely on motion for meaning
- One canonical visible component per screen/role; adapters only when they mount that component
- One stylesheet (`tabletop.css`) owns Blackjack table geometry; no Classic CSS in the active bundle

## Rejected presentation (do not restore)

CSS diamond-hatch wallpaper felt, decorative 2px ellipse rail as finished anatomy, dashed-circle chips, kidney/spatial Dealer plaques on the Dealer board, `data-arc` / `data-dealer-positions` as visual contracts, duplicated Dealer identity in header and felt, PhaseZero admin ledger as a second Dealer screen path, padded “Open seat” / minimum-row Dealer placeholders, 2×2 Blackjack payout button grids, separate `TableCloth` bottom plaque, nested felt panels, giant bordered Player-list spreadsheet.

Dealer Blackjack uses full-width per-box overlay bars (`DealerLedgerRow`) on `BlackjackTableSurface`. Player Blackjack keeps betting boxes on the same surface.

## Tests

Behavioural tests protect commands, legal actions, balances, roles, overflow, and accessibility. They must **not** freeze rejected DOM/class names or Classic-only selectors as Tabletop requirements.
